WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.790
2018 is shaping up to feature a bumper crop
of films, capable of winning over the hearts

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:10.120
of audiences and critics alike, using craftsmanship
and artistry along with the usual loads of

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.790
action and spectacle.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:16.560
From quirky historical comedies to unexpectedly
brilliant animated offerings, these are the

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.270
very best films 2018 has to offer so far.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.460
Thoroughbreds

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.020
Young actress Anya Taylor-Joy has been busy
carving out a niche for herself as a modern-day

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:31.070
scream queen, earning starring roles in critically
acclaimed fright flicks The Witch and Split

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.550
in just the last few years.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:37.350
So, it's no surprise first-time writer-director
Cory Finley recruited her for his debut black

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.289
comedy-thriller Thoroughbreds.

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:43.719
And with the help of his clockwork script
and understated, tension-generating direction,

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:46.170
he was able to score a winner on his first
outing.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:51.359
The plot follows a pair of reuniting friends
as they scheme to assassinate one's stepfather,

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:55.929
and critics were impressed with Finley's ability
to bring a classical feel to the film, which

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.540
had a nice balance of darkness and humor about
it.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.360
"The technique."

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.740
"Holy s---."

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.760
After Thoroughbreds, it's clear auteur Cory
Finley will be one to watch.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.730
Annihilation

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:20.410
Writer-director Alex Garland has made a name
for himself with dark, cerebral sci-fi thrillers

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.660
that aim for a realm beyond simple entertainment.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:28.740
After penning the screenplays for such well-received
flicks as 28 Days Later and Dredd, he made

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:34.910
his directorial debut in 2015 with Ex Machina,
which earned him his first Academy Award nomination

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.700
and a whole lot of interest in what would
come next.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.740
His sophomore feature Annihilation proved
that the buzz surrounding his first outing

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.310
was not a fluke.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:48.470
Adapted from Jeff VanderMeer's 2014 novel,
the mind-blowing, genre-subverting story makes

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:53.900
good use of Garland's talent for atmosphere
- not to mention its roundly excellent cast.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.310
Headed up by Natalie Portman and featuring
Tessa Thompson, Oscar Isaac, and Jennifer

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:03.970
Jason Leigh, Annihilation follows a team of
scientists who dare to explore the Shimmer,

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:08.860
an anomalous area in which the very concept
of reality doesn't seem to apply.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.510
The film received massive praise for its stunning
visuals and sweeping metaphors, and it was

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:18.099
celebrated for being a film that challenged
expectations that left viewers perplexed and

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:20.550
still massively entertained.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.739
Isle of Dogs

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:26.590
Animated films don't get much quirkier than
Isle of Dogs, a stop-motion feature from the

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.090
King of Cinematic Quirk, Wes Anderson.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.409
The film follows a young Japanese boy in a
near-future dystopia on the hunt for his dog,

00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:38.769
who - along with all other dogs - has been
quarantined on an island after an outbreak

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:39.769
of disease.

00:02:39.769 --> 00:02:45.220
The film features voice performances by Bryan
Cranston, Ed Norton, Frances McDormand, Harvey

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.510
Keitel, Tilda Swinton, and Yoko Ono, to name
just a few.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:54.189
Apart from a few stray dissenters, reviewers
were generally won over by the phenomenal

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:57.540
work of the cast and by the film's meticulous
artistry.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.940
"Thank you."

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.670
Even if Anderson's works aren't necessarily
your cup of tea, Isle of Dogs is a must-watch

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:10.040
- if for no other reason than to witness Bryan
Cranston channeling Walter White in dog form.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.040
"Me?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.389
Uh, I don't care."

00:03:13.389 --> 00:03:15.129
Love, Simon

00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:19.790
Whether or not it was any good, Love, Simon
was destined to be important, since it was

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.090
the first major studio Hollywood film to focus
on a gay teen romance.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.700
Fortunately, director Greg Berlanti delivered
a film that's notable for more than just that

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:34.209
reason - it's also a funny, disarmingly sweet
rom-com that had audiences bawling and laughing

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:35.209
out loud.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:40.680
Working from a 2015 YA novel, the script is
populated with strongly drawn characters,

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.239
and actor Nick Robinson earns praise for his
leading role among a cast that includes Jennifer

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:48.180
Garner, Josh Duhamel, and Alexandra Shipp.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:54.419
The film has been noted for its modern soundtrack,
diverse cast, and uplifting, feel-good storyline.

00:03:54.419 --> 00:03:55.749
Journey's End

00:03:55.749 --> 00:04:01.249
This 90-year-old World War I story about British
officers pinned down in a dugout over several

00:04:01.249 --> 00:04:04.510
days has been brought to the screen many times
over.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.279
But while Journey's End might not seem like
the kind of movie that might interest modern

00:04:08.279 --> 00:04:14.450
audiences, director Saul Dibb and screenwriter
Simon Reade, along with an amazing cast, have

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:18.750
crafted it into a meditation on war and death
that feels surprisingly timely.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:24.250
Asa Butterfield stars as Raleigh, a young
officer under the command of Sam Claflin's

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:28.840
alcoholic and unstable Captain Stanhope, as
the soldier grapples with what it means to

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.360
follow orders under the specter of near-certain
doom.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.979
Claflin's performance was widely praised,
as was that of Paul Bettany as a mild-mannered

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:39.630
officer who exhibits grace under pressure.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.449
The film's period production design was also
deemed excellent, as was Dibb's command of

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:46.060
mood and atmosphere.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:50.789
It might be a movie we've seen plenty of before,
but Journey's End is still as riveting today

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:54.210
as it was in its original incarnation.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.370
The Death of Stalin

00:04:56.370 --> 00:05:01.620
Scottish writer-director Armando Iannucci
is perhaps best-known stateside for his work

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.520
on the HBO series Veep, and he's taken that
penchant for political satire to a whole new

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.740
realm with The Death of Stalin.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.650
This adaptation of a French graphic novel
provides an inside look at the chaos, humor,

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:16.030
and horror surrounding the demise of the Russian
dictator.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.379
"How old are you?"

00:05:17.379 --> 00:05:18.379
"I'm old."

00:05:18.379 --> 00:05:19.389
"You are not old!

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:22.080
You're not even a person, you're a testicle!"

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.320
It may seem an unlikely subject for a farce
- but the pitch-black comedy has been garnering

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:32.569
the kind of eye-popping reviews normally reserved
for prestige pictures, with some reviewers

00:05:32.569 --> 00:05:35.099
labeling it a masterpiece.

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:39.470
Featuring a stellar international cast which
includes Steve Buscemi as Nikita Khrushchev

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.919
and Michael Palin as the title tyrant, the
ambitious film hit the sweet spot with critics

00:05:44.919 --> 00:05:48.830
who praised it for being surprisingly timely
and whip-smart.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.509
A Quiet Place

00:05:50.509 --> 00:05:55.270
John Krasinski might be best known for his
comedic timing in The Office, but he's proven

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:59.970
himself to be much more than just quick-witted,
thanks to his directorial debut of the unnerving

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.210
original horror film A Quiet Place.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:08.000
Directing from a screenplay by the writing
team of Scott Beck and Bryan Woods, Krasinski

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.849
stars alongside his real-life wife Emily Blunt
in the tale of a family plagued by mysterious

00:06:12.849 --> 00:06:18.889
creatures which hunt using sound, forcing
their family into a tense and silent existence.

00:06:18.889 --> 00:06:24.030
The film has been widely praised for its daring
conceptual framework and the cast's creative

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.889
and strong performances.

00:06:25.889 --> 00:06:30.740
Most importantly, the film is searingly bleak
and maddeningly scary, so even beyond its

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:35.620
pure ambition, the movie is a treat for horror
junkies of all stripes.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.659
Black Panther

00:06:36.659 --> 00:06:41.650
After ten years of blockbuster features, it's
no surprise that Marvel Studios is still churning

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:47.479
out quality superhero movies, but Black Panther
took things to a new level altogether.

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:52.060
Director Ryan Coogler joined forces with writing
partner Joe Robert Cole to create a story

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:56.620
that, with star Chadwick Boseman in the lead,
managed to surpass even the highest creative

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:02.539
expectations and stunned even the most optimistic
box office watchers with its massive ticket

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:03.539
sales.

00:07:03.539 --> 00:07:07.659
The film has been heralded for its importance
to black audiences in offering a representative

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:12.960
hero and celebrating African culture, and
on top of that, the story structure was astonishingly

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:13.960
good.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.669
Black Panther explores themes of alienation
and loss more effectively than a comic book

00:07:18.669 --> 00:07:23.629
film has any right to - particularly by way
of Michael B. Jordan's conflicted villain

00:07:23.629 --> 00:07:29.400
Erik "Killmonger" Stevens, who has been cited
as the MCU's best villain ever thanks largely

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.120
to Jordan's towering performance.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.889
Paddington 2

00:07:33.889 --> 00:07:38.360
Based on the beloved children's character,
the first Paddington film was a surprise critical

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:41.229
darling and a moderate hit at the box office.

00:07:41.229 --> 00:07:45.969
Its success made a follow-up inevitable, but
Paddington 2 does not suffer the sequel slump

00:07:45.969 --> 00:07:50.939
- thus far, the film has not earned a single
negative review, which gives it the rare distinction

00:07:50.939 --> 00:07:53.760
of a 100 percent rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.130
Some reviewers couldn't help but marvel at
the fact that the film outdid even its formidable

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.150
predecessor.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:04.210
With the talented Ben Whishaw reprising the
title role alongside an appropriately British

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:10.110
cast that includes Hugh Grant in many, many
disguises, Paddington 2 ramps up the whimsy,

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:14.289
adventure, and earnestness of the original
- and with comparable box office returns,

00:08:14.289 --> 00:08:16.849
a third installment is all but assured.

00:08:16.849 --> 00:08:19.280
Avengers: Infinity War

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:24.229
Even the eye-popping box office success of
Black Panther was only a warm up act for Avengers:

00:08:24.229 --> 00:08:29.319
Infinity War, which has shattered as many
box office records as it did hearts.

00:08:29.319 --> 00:08:34.409
As the first part of the culmination of Marvel's
three phase mega-arc, the powerful Infinity

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:39.349
Stones are collected by the Mad Titan Thanos
with the goal of eradicating half of all life

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:40.630
in the universe.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:44.910
Infinity War brought together nearly every
important character introduced in the MCU

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:49.430
thus far - and fans responded by putting up
the kind of box office numbers which made

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:52.440
it one of the top worldwide hits of all time.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:57.240
While the movie didn't earn the widespread
critical adoration enjoyed by Black Panther,

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:03.010
positive reviews recognized it as a singularly
Herculean feat of storytelling, one which

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:07.260
takes time to deliver meaningful arcs for
characters we've come to know and love over

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.170
the years - and, notably, for its villain.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:14.680
Josh Brolin's motion-capture performance as
Thanos moved some critics to declare the Mad

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:20.700
Titan the MCU's best villain ever, and - especially
given the film's amazingly dark cliffhanger

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:25.360
ending - the only one to ever pose a true
threat to Earth's Mightiest Heroes.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.430
Said ending was a sticking point for some
reviewers, who dubbed it a half-movie, but

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:34.460
perhaps their tune will change when the as-yet
untitled Avengers 4 debuts in May of next

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.460
year.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:36.460
Tully

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:40.870
Jason Reitman is a man who knows his way around
thoughtful, engaging comedy.

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.750
The director of hits such as Thank You For
Smoking, Juno, and Up in the Air returned

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:49.230
in 2018 with Tully, which reunited him with
screenwriter Diablo Cody.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:54.139
With her famously quippy dialogue, the story
centers on Charlize Theron's overburdened

00:09:54.139 --> 00:09:59.300
mother figure, who forms an unexpected bond
with her unusual nanny, played by Mackenzie

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.300
Davis.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.339
While even positive reviews were quick to
point out the screenplay's contrivances, critics

00:10:04.339 --> 00:10:09.750
were uniformly won over by another outstanding
performance from Theron, whose comedic chops

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.360
and chemistry with Davis carried the film.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:16.380
Even negative reviews had to give the actress
credit for her passion and skill, and most

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:20.839
reviewers agreed that Tully was a welcome
return for the dream team of Cody and Reitman.

00:10:20.839 --> 00:10:24.900
While the film may not have burned up the
box office, it seems like a candidate for

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.940
a strong second life once released to video.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.889
Deadpool 2

00:10:29.889 --> 00:10:34.820
Fans of Ryan Reynolds' Merc With a Mouth eagerly
awaited the sequel to 2016's ridiculously

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:39.760
huge, comparatively low-budget R-rated hit
Deadpool - and Reynolds, along with incoming

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.519
director David Leitch didn't disappoint.

00:10:41.519 --> 00:10:44.410
"You know, you're a lot taller in the-"

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.959
"Shut up, you little a--hole."

00:10:45.959 --> 00:10:49.769
Those who were even vaguely familiar with
the original knew what they could expect in

00:10:49.769 --> 00:10:54.660
terms of insane action and over-the-top vulgarity,
particularly with the introduction of the

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:59.029
time-traveling cyborg Cable - but many of
them weren't ready for the surprising amount

00:10:59.029 --> 00:11:02.459
of character building and emotion brought
along this time around.

00:11:02.459 --> 00:11:08.040
Zazie Beetz and Josh Brolin both arrived as
immediate fan favorites, and Deadpool's assembly

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:12.790
of the mutant superhero team X-Force is said
to give the new series a stronger foothold

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:16.720
in franchise land and an emotional payoff
that surpasses its predecessor.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:22.250
It's the rare sequel that lives up to, let
alone surpasses the original, but some critics

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:26.610
are calling Deadpool 2 a cut above the phenomenal
first run.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:28.760
"Ooh, I s--- my pants."

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:31.230
"Actually, that may have been me."

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:32.329
Thanks for watching!

00:11:32.329 --> 00:11:34.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:37.319
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

